From e514092bc7c5aad75e82d30a8fa18a50ef8d82cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:04:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.devices.display: Add DisplayMonitor statics.

Implement Windows.Devices.Display.DisplayMonitor's IDisplayMonitorStatics:
GetDeviceSelector(), FromIdAsync() and FromInterfaceIdAsync(), backed by the
monitor device nodes win32u already creates and the SetupAPI interface
enumeration, so the selector, both identifier forms and the returned object
agree with what SetupAPI reports.

The returned IDisplayMonitor exposes only what is known:

- identity, display name (the EDID product name when the EDID is valid),
  adapter and target identifiers, and the connection and connector kinds
  from the properties win32u keeps for the monitor;
- native resolution, physical size, chromaticity, luminance and usage kind
  from a validated EDID, with DisplayID taking precedence over the base
  block. Chromaticities are only reported when all four points are in range,
  and a DisplayID section with trailing non-zero filler or a reserved
  product use is ignored;
- GetDescriptor() returns a copy of exactly the validated EDID blocks, or
  the DisplayID section.

Anything not provided is reported as unavailable instead of being guessed,
and an EDID that the driver synthesized because the display had none is not
treated as the display's descriptor. IDisplayMonitor2 is not implemented.

Resolution takes the display_device_init session mutex that win32u holds
while it rebuilds the monitor nodes, and fails if the lock cannot be taken,
so each object is built from a single display configuration. Only monitors
with an enabled interface resolve.

The tests cover the factory and interface identity, selector against SetupAPI,
both identifier forms, removal races, asynchronous completion, valid,
truncated and malformed descriptors and DisplayID sections, base EDID facts,
the connector mappings and the synthesized EDID case, using test-owned monitor
device nodes under Wine.
